<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Massing Bill — worked demo</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
    margin: 0 auto; max-width: 62rem; padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem;
  }
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1rem; letter-spacing: .04em; margin: 3rem 0 .75rem;
       opacity: .7; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.1rem; opacity: .8; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .93rem; margin: 1rem 0; width: 100%; }
  th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,.3); padding: .5rem .6rem;
           text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  thead th { font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .04em; opacity: .7; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
  th.num { text-align: right; }
  .ok { color: #1a7f37; }
  .bad { color: #a4262c; }
  .links a { margin-right: .5rem; }
  .facts { display: grid; gap: .3rem 1.5rem; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
           margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .facts dt { opacity: .65; }
  .facts dd { margin: 0; }
  .note { background: rgba(128,128,128,.09); border-left: 3px solid rgba(128,128,128,.5);
          font-size: .9rem; padding: .8rem 1rem; }
  .disclaimer { border-top: 1px solid rgba(128,128,128,.3); font-size: .8rem;
                margin-top: 3rem; opacity: .7; padding-top: 1rem; }
  code { background: rgba(128,128,128,.15); border-radius: 4px;
         font-size: .9em; padding: .1em .35em; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Massing Bill — worked demo</h1>
<p class="lede">
  Six months of billing on a {{ contract_sum }} medical office building, produced
  by the real engine. Every figure below came out of the same code a self-hoster
  runs; none of it is mocked up.
</p>

<dl class="facts">
  <dt>Project</dt>
  <dd>{{ project_number }} — {{ project_name }}</dd>
  <dt>Jurisdiction</dt>
  <dd>California — retention capped at 5% on private works (SB 61, eff. 2026-01-01)</dd>
  <dt>Contract sum</dt>
  <dd>{{ contract_sum }} on 12 lines across 9 CSI divisions</dd>
  <dt>Built</dt>
  <dd>{{ built_on }}</dd>
</dl>

<h2>What the six periods demonstrate</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>1&ndash;2</strong> &mdash; first billing and steady progress.</li>
  <li><strong>3</strong> &mdash; a change order adds a new schedule line mid-stream.</li>
  <li><strong>4</strong> &mdash; bonded off-site curtain wall appears in column F.</li>
  <li><strong>5</strong> &mdash; it installs: column F empties into column E, billed
      once, not twice.</li>
  <li><strong>6</strong> &mdash; a deductive change order, and the architect certifies
      $18,000 less than was applied for. The next period&rsquo;s line 7 follows the
      certificate, not the request.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Applications</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th class="num">No.</th>
      <th>Period</th>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th class="num">Completed &amp; stored</th>
      <th class="num">Certified</th>
      <th>Reconciliation</th>
      <th>Documents</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {%- for page in pages %}
    <tr>
      <td class="num">{{ page.number }}</td>
      <td>{{ page.period }}</td>
      <td>{{ page.status }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ page.completed }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ page.certified }}</td>
      <td class="{{ 'ok' if page.tieout_ok else 'bad' }}">{{ page.tieout }}</td>
      <td class="links">
        <a href="{{ page.files.html }}">view</a>
        {%- for label, path in page.downloads %}
        <a href="{{ path }}">{{ label }}</a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </td>
    </tr>
  {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="note">
  Every period carries one warning: the subcontractor&rsquo;s Form W-9 is not on
  file. That is on purpose. A warning is a thing the project manager should know
  and can still bill through; an <em>error</em> blocks submission outright. A
  demo where everything is clean would not show you the difference.
</p>

{% if not pdf_available %}
<p class="note">
  PDF output is absent from this build: the native WeasyPrint stack was not
  installed on the machine that produced it.
</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>The reconciliation page</h2>
<p>
  Every rendered application carries one. It is the thing no competitor ships:
  each of the G702 lines and G703 columns checked against the contract, the
  schedule of values and the preceding period, with the failures named
  <em>before</em> the owner sees them. Open any application above and scroll to
  the last page.
</p>

<h2>The spreadsheet is the honest one</h2>
<p>
  Download an <code>.xlsx</code> above and click a cell in column G. It is
  <code>=E6+F6+G6</code>, not a number. The cover sheet references the
  continuation sheet&rsquo;s totals rather than restating them. A spreadsheet of
  frozen figures asks to be trusted; one of formulas can be checked.
</p>

<h2>Lien waivers</h2>
<p>
  Twelve states prescribe the exact wording of a lien waiver, and a form that
  does not substantially conform can be unenforceable. This build ships
  <strong>{{ unverified }} statutory templates with empty bodies</strong>, and the
  renderer refuses them by name and citation until someone reads the statute and
  enters the verbatim text. Inventing plausible statutory language would release
  lien rights nobody would discover were gone until the money was.
</p>
{% if waiver_refusal %}
<p class="note">{{ waiver_refusal }}</p>
{% endif %}

<p><a href="https://github.com/MassingCloud/massingbill">Source, and how to run it
yourself &rarr;</a></p>

<p class="disclaimer">
  Prepared with Massing Bill. Format follows the AIA G702/G703 line structure.
  Massing Bill is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by The American
  Institute of Architects. AIA&reg;, G702&reg; and G703&reg; are registered
  trademarks of the AIA. The parties, amounts and dates on these pages are
  fictitious.
</p>

</body>
</html>
